    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d895">

                <pb facs="0959" n="1793" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/268</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-28T10:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 24 [<hi rendition="#italic">23</hi>], 2 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >7</hi>] p.m. I saw the Minister of Foreign Affairs this afternoon and took
                    up with him in conversation the matter of the status in Argentine ports of the
                    Dutch ships now taken over by United States, according to instructions conveyed
                    to me in the telegram above referred to.</p>
                <p>The Minister of Foreign Affairs assured me definitely that when such vessels
                    arrive in Argentine ports they will be considered as being the property of the
                    United States, as national vessels, and that <pb facs="0960" n="1794"
                        xml:id="pg1794"/> the Argentine Government will neither make nor permit to
                    be made any inquiry as to their former ownership; that since this is the
                    attitude of the Government the courts in this country must adopt the same
                    attitude in the event of any attempt to attach them by legal means. To confirm
                    this promise the Minister informed me that he would address a note to me on this
                    question reiterating these assurances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
